  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "OpenAI classifies GPT-5.4 mini as below High in biochemical, cybersecurity, and AI self-improvement under the Preparedness Framework.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "33",
        "pdfPage": 34,
        "quote": "Based on our Preparedness evaluations, we have determined that GPT-5.4 mini as below High"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "GPT-5.4 mini has lower chain of thought (CoT) controllability than any prior model for which OpenAI reported CoT controllability; Figure 18 has no extractable numbers in text.", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "32",
        "pdfPage": 33,
        "quote": "has lower CoT controllability than any previous model we reported CoT controllability for."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Biology capabilities are treated as closely comparable to GPT-5; mini is not Bio High despite receiving full biological-risk safety training.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "34",
        "pdfPage": 35,
        "quote": "it, too, is not High under our Preparedness Framework. Nonetheless, GPT-5-4 mini received our"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A physical-world novice virology randomized controlled trial (RCT) found only modest large language model (LLM) benefit (5.2% LLM vs 6.6% internet completion) and informed treating GPT-5 as below Bio High.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "34",
        "pdfPage": 35,
        "quote": "workflow: completion was 5.2% in the LLM arm versus 6.6% in the internet arm. The paper’s"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Even under refusal-inclusive scoring, automated bio evals are judged insufficient to put mini over Bio High where GPT-5 is not.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "35",
        "pdfPage": 36,
        "quote": "basis to conclude that GPT-5.4 mini crosses the Bio High threshold where GPT-5 does not. The"
      }
